From 0316cd887383a211fedb3f1b192f5d18a566d00f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bvchess <53128914+bvchess@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:16:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] A search from a floor: search::search_floor, the command
 taxman floor N SCORE, and the tests of the floor lemma (R5)

search_forgetting takes a floor, a promotion sum: with one it makes no start and runs the engine from an incumbent worth
the floor whose set is empty, with no seed and no finder.  SearchResult::floor_held says that the search completed with
nothing above the floor, and the end and resume_point take the empty set worth the floor as that incumbent.  The
checkpoint header records the floor, so a checkpoint resumes only under its own floor, and one of a search from a start
under none.

solver::floor sets the board up as solve does (prepare_search, now shared with set_up_with_width), searches from SCORE
less in_the_bag, keeps its checkpoint and clock as a game of solve does, checks the outcome against the replay and the
built-in table, and writes no results line; taxman floor prints what it came to, and the moves of a game that beats the
floor.

Tests: on every game of the Java's to 400 that needs a search, a floor below P* finds it and one at P* or above holds,
at once from the root's bound (one thread; four threads and without the rule of symmetric pairs on a sample); a floor
at P* searches the tree of the search seeded with an optimal set, step for step (800, and 1000 in a release run); a
floor at a ceiling ends before the search starts; a stopped search from a floor resumes under its own floor only; the
header round trip with a floor; and the command: it holds at opt(800), is beaten one below it by opt(800), stops and
resumes, and solve and another floor refuse its checkpoint.  Docs: tests.md (R5), trust.md, search.md, REFERENCE.md
and the glossary.

On-disk format: the checkpoint header is version 9, 47 bytes, with a byte and a u64 for the floor after the tactics;
checkpoints of earlier builds are refused, as at every change of version.  The probe's windows are made again (perf
make-window 992 1024 and 1215 1024), and the probe's fingerprint stays aff672d2dccda0dc, with the windows' steps and
fingerprints unchanged.
